  "content": "Here is the step-by-step exact integer arithmetic for the given problem.\n\n**Given values:**\n*   $a = 137$\n*   $b = 29$\n*   $c = 11$\n\n**Expression to compute:**\n$$ (a \\times b + c^3) - (a - b) \\times c $$\n\n### Step 1: Compute $a \\times b$\n$$ 137 \\times 29 $$\nBreak down $29$ into $30 - 1$:\n$$ 137 \\times 30 = 4110 $$\n$$ 137 \\times 1 = 137 $$\n$$ 4110 - 137 = 2973 $$\nSo, $a \\times b = 2973$.\n\n### Step 2: Compute $c^3$\n$$ 11^3 = 11 \\times 11 \\times 11 $$\n$$ 11 \\times 11 = 121 $$\n$$ 121 \\times 11 = 1331 $$\nSo, $c^3 = 1331$.\n\n### Step 3: Compute the first parenthesis $(a \\times b + c^3)$\n$$ 2973 + 1331 $$\nAdd the integers:\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n& 2973 \\\\\n+& 1331 \\\\\n\\hline\n& 4304\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\nSo, $(a \\times b + c^3) = 4304$.\n\n### Step 4: Compute $(a - b)$\n$$ 137 - 29 $$\n$$ 137 - 29 = 108 $$\nSo, $(a - b) = 108$.\n\n### Step 5: Compute the second parenthesis part $(a - b) \\times c$\n$$ 108 \\times 11 $$\nBreak down $11$ into $10 + 1$:\n$$ 108 \\times 10 = 1080 $$\n$$ 108 \\times 1 = 108 $$\n$$ 1080",
